package ex

// `==` on an expanding self-application: every comparator's nested
// recipe instantiates a strictly larger W, so no finite set of
// generated comparators covers it. The mint budget reports E0906 at
// the `==` site instead of hanging (previously `gom build` diverged).
// The fixture lives in a subdirectory because the checker's own
// bounded expansion walk makes it a multi-second input — inside the
// FuzzCompile sandbox's 8s race-mode budget it would read as a hang,
// and the seed glob only covers testdata/spec/*.gom.
type W a = {next: List (W (W a))}

fn eq (x: W Int) (y: W Int) -> Bool = x == y
